returns.withdrawalPeriod:
The withdrawal period is 14 days from the day,

- on which you or a third party named by you, who is not the carrier, have taken or has taken possession of the goods, provided that you have ordered one or more goods under a single order and these are delivered uniformly;

- on which you or a third party named by you, who is not the carrier, have taken or has taken possession of the last item, provided that you have ordered several goods under a single order and these are delivered separately;

- on which you or a third party named by you, who is not the carrier, have taken or has taken possession of the last partial shipment or the last item, provided that you have ordered a good that is delivered in several partial shipments or pieces.

returns.exclusionsText:
The right of withdrawal does not exist for contracts
- for the delivery of goods that are not prefabricated and for the manufacture of which an individual selection or determination by the consumer is decisive or which are clearly tailored to the personal needs of the consumer;
- for the delivery of goods that can spoil quickly or whose expiration date would quickly be exceeded;
- for the delivery of newspapers, periodicals or magazines with the exception of subscription contracts.

The right of withdrawal expires prematurely for contracts
- for the delivery of sealed goods that are not suitable for return for reasons of health protection or hygiene if their seal has been removed after delivery;
- for the delivery of goods if, due to their nature, they have been inseparably mixed with other goods after delivery;
- for the delivery of sound or video recordings or computer software in a sealed package, if the seal has been removed after delivery.
